---
description: |
  Indexes SOC Prime Active Threats by Sigma rule ID.

  The operator expects OSINT Inventory Info events from `socprime::ocsf::map`
  and emits one event per Sigma rule ID in `uid`, the ID that detection
  findings carry in `finding_info.analytic.uid`. `threats` lists the OCSF
  `osint` objects of all Active Threats that the rule belongs to.

  A High-Order Sigma rule describes the attack chain of its threat, so its
  entry holds the complete `osint` object. A behavior rule often belongs to
  several threats and its findings alone do not attribute an attack, so its
  entry only references the threats by `uid`, `value`, and `src_url`.
---

where class_uid == 5021
unroll osint
_analytic = osint.related_analytics
unroll _analytic
_threat = osint if _analytic.category == "High-Order Sigma" else {
  type_id: osint.type_id,
  type: osint.type,
  uid: osint.uid,
  value: osint.value,
  src_url: osint.src_url,
  vendor_name: osint.vendor_name,
}
summarize uid=_analytic.uid, threats=collect(_threat)
